    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5855" root="جشع" body-key="j">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَشِعٌ</span></b>  part. n. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَشِعَ</span>, <i>Affected with the most
vehement desire,</i> &amp;c.: pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَشِعُونَ</span>, (S, K,) and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَشَاعَى</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جُشَعَآءَ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جِشَاعٌ</span> are also pls. [of the
same]. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الجَشِعُ</span> <i>The lion.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَجُلٌ جَشِعٌ بَشِعٌ</span>, <i>A man in whom are combined
impatience and fright and a heavy,</i> or <i>a heaving,
state of the soul.</i> (TA.)

